// Issue #1614: ByteCodeGenerator: combined stack layout causes out-of-frame register writes
//
// ScriptParser::generateCodeBlockTreeFromASTWalkerPostProcess validated
// m_identifierOnStackCount, m_identifierOnHeapCount, and
// m_lexicalBlockStackAllocatedIdentifierMaximumDepth against VARIABLE_LIMIT
// separately, but never validated their sum. ByteCodeGenerator::relocateByteCode
// assumes registers at or above stackBase+VARIABLE_LIMIT belong to a distinct
// register class and relocates them using totalStackAllocatedVariableSize()
// (= identifierOnStackCount + lexicalBlockStackAllocatedIdentifierMaximumDepth).
// When both counts are individually within VARIABLE_LIMIT but their sum exceeds
// it, the relocated register index crosses block->m_requiredTotalRegisterNumber.
// The bounds check is an ASSERT, compiled out in release builds, so a plain
// `registerFile[code->m_registerIndex1] = ...` writes out of the allocated
// register frame with an attacker-influenced value.
//
// poc() below declares ~16000 function-scoped `var`s (identifierOnStackCount)
// and, in a nested block, ~16000 `let`s (lexicalBlockStackAllocatedIdentifierMaximumDepth).
// Each count individually stays under VARIABLE_LIMIT (16383) but their sum
// does not. Before the fix this crosses the relocation invariant (visible as
// an ASSERT failure in debug builds, an unchecked OOB register write in
// release builds). After the fix, the combined layout is rejected with a
// SyntaxError before bytecode generation.
